  "manual": {
    "notes": [
      "Trenton, NJ: Fitzgerald's 1919 directory — 'Albertson Edwin S, boilermaker, h 1041 Liberty' with Howard (wireworker — this is direct ancestor Howard I Albertson), Walter M (U.S. Army) and Clara E (operator) at the same address. Industrial work explains the family's move from Camden County to Trenton, made between his father Isaac's death (1896) and the 1910 census.",
      "The ancestral homestead never passed through this branch: after John Albertson's death (1842) his son Chalkley bought out the co-heirs; on Chalkley's death (1880) it went to Chalkley's sons Charles S. and John J. The 'Albertson' locality name near Magnolia comes from Chalkley's farm (railroad stop arranged with Samuel Richards at Chalkley's house, 1877); the 1743/1865 house still stands near W. Evesham Road."
    ]
  }
